# omni-code Project Conventions

## TypeScript
- Use strict TypeScript throughout — avoid `any` except where genuinely necessary
- Always add `.js` extension on imports in main-process files (Electron ESM requirement)
- Use `type` imports for type-only references
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/intersections

## Electron Architecture
- Main process code lives in `main/` — no DOM APIs here
- Renderer process code lives in `renderer/` — no Node.js APIs here
- All cross-process communication goes through `main/preload.ts` via `contextBridge`
- IPC handlers follow the `namespace:action` pattern (e.g. `rules:list`, `agent:send-message`)

## React / Renderer
- Use Zustand stores (`renderer/stores/`) for shared state
- Use functional components with hooks only
- CSS classes use kebab-case; follow the existing `settings-*`, `rule-*` naming patterns
- Import CSS directly into the component file that uses it

## File Naming
- Main-process files: `kebab-case.ts` in `main/`
- Renderer components: `PascalCase.tsx` in `renderer/components/`
- Stores: `camelCaseStore.ts` in `renderer/stores/`

## Agent / Core
- Tool names in `src/tools/builtin/` use PascalCase class names
- New IPC handlers must be registered in both `setupIpcHandlers()` (or a sibling setup fn) and `cleanupIpcHandlers()`
- System prompt additions are injected in `main/core-integration.ts:buildSystemPrompt()`
